<h2 id="remaining-checkpoints">Remaining checkpoints</h2>
<p>B02 and B04 are locally verified with independent review. B05 is in progress; B03/B06 have not started. Full B15 privacy integration includes out-of-scope dependencies and cannot be completed by this authorization alone. The17 skipped-test registry remains mandatory. Live cleanup, backup location/retention approval, production verification and any rollout remain pending and prohibited in this run.</p>
<h2 id="b02-disposition">B02 disposition</h2>
<p>01-T02/03/04 have local implementation, behavioral RED, relevant owning-package GREEN, independent source review, and real demo Firestore transaction/Rules evidence. This permits the B04 code dependency handoff. It is not WO-01 completion, live-data acceptance or finding closure. The approved C01 private deletion/legacy conflict protocol supersedes the earlier planning ambiguity. <code>admin-content.js</code> required no change because its existing validator already accepts and validates the mixed editable input; the storage partition is enforced at the shared save boundary.</p>
<h2 id="b04-disposition-and-evidence-correction">B04 disposition and evidence correction</h2>
<p>01-T07/08 have independent source approval and a separate independent Node22 run of 82 focused tests. The current validator rejects nested malformed field values and unknown roots before IO, while preserving Date and trusted SDK timestamp support without a new dependency. No seed or sync main entry point was executed against Firebase.</p>
<ul><li>Original writer RED: 52 tests, 10 pass, 42 intended missing-rejection failures (<code>B04-writers-red.log</code>).</li><li>Residual RED: <code>B04-types-red.log</code> contains 12 valid intended failures and 3 invalid fixture counter mismatches. The latter do not count as RED evidence.</li><li>Corrected stats tests: 3 intended missing-exception failures against an isolated reconstruction of the prior top-level validator (<code>B04-stats-controlled-red.log</code>). This is a controlled pre-fix reproduction, not a contemporaneous baseline run. Exact source, hashes and provenance: <code>B04-stats-red-provenance.json</code>. The working source was never reverted.</li><li>Corrected focused GREEN: 82 passed, zero skips (<code>B04-types-green.log</code>). Seed package: 33 passed (<code>B04-seed-package-green.log</code>). Functions: 192 passed, zero skips; lint passed (<code>B04-functions-green.log</code>, <code>B04-functions-lint.log</code>).</li><li>Source-projection import/restore guards are not represented as real Firestore integration tests.</li></ul>
<p>This permits the B05 dependency handoff; R01/R10 remain OPEN.</p>
<h2 id="resumed-baseline-and-b05-status">Resumed baseline and B05 status</h2>
<p>On 2026-10-26 the refreshed checkout is clean at <code>f3c9485</code>, which contains the existing WO-01 work and B05 producer changes. This run did not create that commit. The B05 producer logs show 33 tests with 16 intended assertion failures before fixes, focused GREEN, 206 full Functions tests passed and lint passed. The shared <code>index.js</code> bootstrap is still unchanged and its actual emulator RED check is pending. B05 is not complete or independently accepted. The interrupted earlier emulator launch produced no result and is not evidence.</p>
<h2 id="b05-t09-callable-verification">B05 T09 callable verification</h2>
<ul><li>Actual demo/Auth/Functions/Firestore RED: 14 tests, 9 passed, 5 failed on profile email creation, backfill or automatic email-derived names (<code>B05-email-red.log</code>). No setup or environment failure counted.</li><li>After the minimal I-owned <code>functions/index.js</code> change, all 14 emulator tests passed, zero skips (<code>B05-email-green.log</code>). Auth email/verification, proof recovery, rate limits and conflict controls remain exercised by the existing suite.</li><li>Exact integrated Functions candidate: 206 passed, zero skips, lint passed (<code>B05-functions-integrated-green.log</code>, <code>B05-functions-integrated-lint.log</code>).</li><li>Independent T09 preliminary review: no concrete introduced bypass/regression; independent focused33/33 passed. Final B05 acceptance still waits for T09a standalone-tool completion and independent review.</li><li>T09a is being tested only with injected synthetic SDK/storage/logs. No migration main entry point has been invoked against Firebase.</li></ul>
<h2 id="b05-disposition">B05 disposition</h2>
<p>B05 passed independent read-only review of T09 and T09a. The reviewer independently ran 33 producer tests and 23 standalone-tool tests, all passing with zero skips; reviewed actual integrated Functions206 and email-emulator14 GREEN logs; and confirmed the intended RED assertions. No introduced bypass or regression was found.</p>
<p>T09a evidence: <code>B05-legacy-red.log</code> (12 tests: 2 pass, 10 intended privacy/default-write failures); <code>B05-legacy-green.log</code> (23 passed, zero skips; 11 additional guards are not RED evidence); <code>B05-legacy-provenance.json</code> records source/test hashes and commands. Syntax and whitespace checks passed.</p>
<p>The standalone tool is import-safe, requires an explicit project/root, defaults to dry-run and requires <code>--apply</code> to write. Its main entry point was not invoked. Existing unbounded source reads, batching and creation races are preserved and do not receive production acceptance. It must remain quiesced during separately approved privacy cleanup. Example preparation-only syntax: <code>node tool/migrate-legacy-users.mjs --project=&lt;explicit-project&gt; --root=HudHudDev</code>; live invocation is not authorized here.</p>
<p>This permits B03 implementation. R01 and R10 remain OPEN, and no production operation is authorized.</p>
<h2 id="b03-stopped-at-mandatory-lint-gate">B03 stopped at mandatory lint gate</h2>
<p>Status: <strong>INCOMPLETE — STOPPED</strong>, as required by the user's instruction to stop on a failed mandatory gate.</p>
<ul><li>T05 baseline RED: 8 intended assertion failures, zero skips (<code>B03-reader-red.log</code>). Focused GREEN: 17 passed, zero skips (<code>B03-reader-green.log</code>). Targeted lint/type checks and emulator-test syntax passed (<code>B03-reader-lint.log</code>). An intermediate test type-inference error was corrected and does not count as RED.</li><li>T06 export baseline RED: 14 tests, 12 passed and 2 intended privacy failures, zero skips (<code>B03-export-red.log</code>). Form/export GREEN: 15 passed, zero skips (<code>B03-export-green.log</code>). New helper guard cases are not claimed as baseline RED.</li><li>Mandatory whole-admin lint <strong>FAILED</strong> (<code>B03-T06-lint.log</code>): <code>web_admin/components/admin/admin-app.tsx:3351</code> calls <code>setPrivateError</code> synchronously inside the new loading effect; the existing React compiler lint rule rejects it.</li><li>No further source fixes or dependent tasks were executed after this failure. B03 has not passed independent batch review or exact-candidate integration gates.</li><li>Next corrective step: derive the unauthorized station-editor error from current authorization instead of setting state synchronously in the effect; retain asynchronous read error handling. Then rerun lint, complete T10/T11 in order, execute the actual admin/Rules emulator gates and owning test/build gates, and obtain independent B03 review. This is proposed work, not a verified fix.</li><li>The new T05 actual emulator cases were authored but <strong>not executed</strong>. Ordinary unit execution or syntax checking does not satisfy them.</li><li>T10/T11 and B06 remain unexecuted. No privacy cleanup apply/restore script, live migration, deployment or protected-branch merge was performed.</li></ul>
